title What an address space is made of -- twelve parts, seven held, and the join the two rings never had
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3426 at the open, so the council rota reads row 3426 mod 5 = 1 -- Air and Saturn, law and boundary: TAME_CORE, single-stranded, and Gauge Style. The single-stranded row governed this lap directly. Its whole argument is that parts which stand free can be drawn out and understood alone, and the finding here is that Caravan's two memory rings stand so free they had never been introduced.
think Every living REDS row reads CLOSED, so no standfast. The three newest logs converge on one recommend: the fourth microkernel rung is the address space, and measure regions.rye and mapping.rye against Microkit's memory-region vocabulary before deciding whether there is a finding or only a transcription.
think Read Microkit's own BSD-2-Clause source rather than its CC-BY-SA manual, since the licence table permits the code and the clean-room discipline reads interface names. tool/microkit/src/sdf/memory_region.rs declares SysMemoryRegion with ten fields and SysMap with five. Two of the ten and one of the five are tool bookkeeping -- text_pos twice, page_size_specified_by_user once -- so twelve parts describe the memory rather than the tool.
think Measured the accounting rather than argued it. Caravan holds seven of the twelve, and the seven split four to regions.rye and three to mapping.rye. Every one of the four is something a person writes down -- a name, a size, which region a grant names, the permissions. Every one of the three is something the machine computes -- page size, page count, virtual address. That is the framework's own line between a declaration and its lowering, and Caravan reached it one bounded ring at a time without reading it anywhere.
think The five owed are one debt rather than five: physical address, region kind, two prefill sources, caching attribute. Each is about the physical world a region lives in, and Caravan has never placed anything in physical memory. Same shape objects.rye found when four mapping objects turned out to be one address space wearing four page sizes.
think The third finding is the one worth the round, and measurement is what produced it. regions.rye asserts a size is at least one byte and at most 16 MiB, with no page-multiple requirement; mapping.rye's Placement.refusal returns unaligned_length for anything the page does not divide. Built a throwaway probe against both modules: of the 8,192 sizes from one byte to 8,192, regions.rye accepts every one and mapping.rye plans exactly two. Two of the four regions regions.rye's own self-test declares -- 2,048 twice -- miss a page boundary.
think Nearly reached for the wrong repair. Requiring page alignment in regions.rye would have been a refusal, and reading the call sites first showed why that is wrong: roundtrip, notify, serve and carry each take their extent from exercise.store_extent, a real file's length, which owes a page nothing. Refusing them would abort on an honest declaration.
think Microkit meets exactly that case and answers it -- a region may be sized by a prefill file, and memory_region.rs:423 rounds the length up to the page size rather than refusing. So the repair is a conversion rather than a restriction, and page_extent is that conversion in Caravan's own words. Reading the data before acting on it is REDS %213's lesson, and it turned a breaking change into an added function.
think Wrote the join as a load-bearing assert rather than a described one. address_space.rye imports regions.rye and mapping.rye and compares their actual constants, so moving either bound past the other reds on the lap that moves it. Proved that from both ends: widening max_region_bytes from 16 MiB to 1 TiB reds at line 480, the join assert; narrowing page_bits from 12 to 13 reds at line 484, the rounding assert. Read the panic traces and confirmed each fires at the assert it claims to test, since a refusal at some other line proves something else.
think The symbol scan compares field ORDER as well as membership, because the module claims to list the parts in the source's own order and a claim about order that only membership is checked against is a claim nothing holds. The moved-field plant is what earns it: two fields swapped keeps field_mismatch at 0 and lifts order_mismatch to 2. refusals.rye once carried the right eleven names with two meanings swapped inside a names-only check (REDS %107).
think Moved all six plants into a control fixture after the third attempt to embed a quoted awk program inside a rishi string failed to parse. That is REDS %85's own loom -- a quoted program interpolated into a shell word is the fragile shape -- and the control is both the cleaner engineering and the seated pattern.
obs Own process red, and it is mine. I started the cold roster in the background and then edited the tree while it was still walking, so it reported caravan_ladder_roster red -- it had reached that guard after address_space.rye existed and before its LADDER row did. A cold reading measures the tree before the lap touches it, and a background run that overlaps the lap is not one. The hot run at the end is the honest measurement; the cold one was contaminated by my own hand.
obs The caravan suite's bijection guard is correct and it fires -- it named caravan_allowances_witness unheard, a lap after that witness landed. Nothing was broken: the guard simply never ran, because caravan_suite_witness stands off the standing roster. That is the already-named class the card carries (1,683 witnesses on disk, 56 gated) showing up in one more room, so both witnesses were registered and the root was named rather than a new red booked.
obs Declined to book the size disagreement as a red, and the reasoning is worth keeping. Nothing is currently producing a wrong answer, because nothing calls across that seam yet -- Caravan has never lowered a declaration onto a kernel. A red is something wrong and a ratchet is something not yet uniform, and booking a red for a seam that has never fired would spend the word that stops the line.
obs GREEN on the first build, for the second lap running, and the reason is the same as last time: every number was measured on metal before a line was written, so the module only had to state what the probe already said. A green that arrives on the first try still deserves the question, which is why the join control exists.
loom witness=caravan_address_space_witness plants=6 plants_bitten=6 join_refusals=2 parts=12 held=7 owed=5
loom probe=regions_mapping_join sizes_tested=8192 accepted_by_regions=8192 planned_by_mapping=2
loom plan=largest_declarable bytes=16777216 pages_best=8 pages_worst=519 plan_bound=2556 tables=2
file caravan/address_space.rye the fourth microkernel rung -- twelve parts, seven held across two rings, and page_extent as the join
file tools/ca/caravan_address_space_witness.rish binds the twelve against Microkit's source and proves eight refusals on metal
file tools/fixtures/caravan_address_space_symbol_scan.sh diffs field names AND order, and names the three bookkeeping exclusions
file tools/fixtures/caravan_address_space_scan_control.sh six plants and one welcome on real files in a throwaway pen
file tools/fixtures/caravan_address_space_join_control.sh proves the join load-bearing twice -- a bound widened and a page narrowed
file caravan/LADDER.md the rung's row, so the ladder table and the caravan directory stay one set
file tools/ca/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers address_space and the allowances witness that had stood off it
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled with the rung and its findings; the landed laps shelved
file construction/archive/20260825-003210_itinerary-landed-laps.md two elder Prior-lap rows shelved rather than dropped
recommend keep-going the address space's five owed parts are one debt and they want a booted kernel rather than more accounting, so the next agent-doable rung is elsewhere -- caravan_suite_witness standing off the standing roster is the smaller crux and it is the same class as REDS %191, one room over; beside it, the ASCII guard reads *.rye alone while .rish and .sh comments sit outside it
